## Scope

Draft integration work for #876 (part 4/5 of #871), stacked on #867 so the current scale-power behavior remains the baseline.

This first slice defines the Decaid-side exact-attempt ownership contract without adding an app-global BLE mutex:

- add `ConnectionAttemptOwner` / `ConnectionAttemptLease` keyed by normalized device id + generation;
- cancellation invalidates only the exact lease and keeps its slot owned until settlement;
- stale cancel/settle cannot affect a replacement generation;
- different device ids remain independent;
- add deterministic unit coverage for cancellation, stale completion, replacement safety, independence and retiring-attempt diagnostics;
- add the part-4 integration audit covering ConnectionManager, quick connect, EarlyConnectWatcher/ScanOrchestrator, ScaleWatch, scan ownership, plugin sessions, timeout chain, retry ownership and fault policy.

## Upstream dependency gate

The provisional #875 direction is the narrow native admission/lifecycle solution in `tadelv/universal_ble` (#26/#27, draft PRs #25/#28).

I am intentionally **not** changing the `universal_ble` pin in this slice. The current reviewed #28 head is `84c5406872d6fbef5ddae57dea0c7dfdfe12d759`, but its Android unit-test job is red with three regressions:

- `NotificationLifecycleTest.staleDisconnectCannotRemoveCurrentGatt`
- `UniversalBlePluginTest.mixedCaseDisconnectKeepsConnectDisconnectDelay`
- `UniversalBlePluginTest.connectedCallbackCancelsPendingReconnect`

The final part-4 pin must use the exact reviewed **green** #28 head in both `pubspec.yaml` and `pubspec.lock`, preserving unrelated pins including `flutter_js`.

## Remaining wiring in this draft

- fence `De1Controller` / `ScaleController` adoption with the exact attempt lease;
- keep caller-timed-out attempts owned until their source + owned cleanup settle;
- make scan cancellation invalidate scan-owned early attempts without cancelling unrelated explicit connects;
- remove/replace the orphan-producing quick-connect outer timeout while keeping a single host retry owner;
- transition watch-owned stop-for-connect through the existing scan-owner state machine;
- add cancellation/timeout/late-success/retry-fairness/watch regressions;
- pin the final green fork SHA and run the focused Flutter/analyze/Android matrix.

## Coordination

Depends on / preserves #867. Uses #875 as the decision/evidence gate and #26/#27 as the native implementation gates. Hardware acceptance remains #877 (part 5/5). This draft does **not** close #871.

